return {h=13,w=390,cr=60,hc=20,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"water2"},st={80,92,65,65,80,68},ab={{33,0},{41,0},{31,1}},genus={en="Goldfish Pokémon",es="Pokémon Pez Color",pt="Pokémon Peixe-dourado"},flavor={en={[1]="In the autumn spawning season, they can be seen swimming powerfully up rivers and creeks.",[2]="In the autumn spawning season, they can be seen swimming powerfully up rivers and creeks.",[3]="It is the male's job to make a nest by carving out boulders in a stream using the horn on its head.",[4]="During spawning season, SEAKING gather from all over, coloring the rivers a brilliant red.",[5]="Using its horn, it bores holes in riverbed boulders, making nests to prevent its eggs from washing away.",[6]="When autumn comes, the males patrol the area around their nests in order to protect their offspring.",[7]="In the autumn, SEAKING males can be seen performing courtship dances in riverbeds to woo females. During this season, this Pokémon’s body coloration is at its most beautiful.",[8]="SEAKING is very protective of its eggs. The male and female will take turns patrolling around their nest and eggs. The guarding of eggs by these Pokémon goes on for over a month.",[9]="It punches holes in boulders on streambeds. This is a clever innovation that prevents its eggs from being attacked or washed away by the current.",[10]="The horn on its head is sharp like a drill. It bores a hole in a boulder to make its nest.",[11]="In the autumn spawning season, they can be seen swimming powerfully up rivers and creeks.",[12]="It makes its nest by hollowing out boulders in streams with its horn. It defends its eggs with its life.",[13]="To protect its family, it will fight with its drill-sharp horn. It lives in hollowed rocks in streams.",[14]="In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.",[15]="During spawning season, SEAKING gather from all over, causing rivers to appear a brilliant red.",[16]="Using its horn, it bores holes in riverbed boulders, making nests to prevent its eggs from washing away.",[17]="In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.",[18]="In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.",[21]="In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.",[22]="In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.",[23]="In the autumn spawning season, they can be seen swimming powerfully up rivers and creeks.",[24]="It makes its nest by hollowing out boulders in streams with its horn. It defends its eggs with its life.",[25]="In the autumn, Seaking males can be seen performing courtship dances in riverbeds to woo females. During this season, this Pokémon’s body coloration is at its most beautiful.",[26]="Seaking is very protective of its eggs. The male and female will take turns patrolling around their nest and eggs. The guarding of eggs by these Pokémon goes on for over a month.",[27]="When the weather grows cold, its whole body flushes a deep red. This sight serves as a poetic reminder that autumn has arrived.",[28]="Trainers who are crazy for Seaking are divided into horn enthusiasts and fin enthusiasts. The two groups do not get along well.",[29]="Its horn spins like a drill to steadily hollow out rocks, even harder ones. The coloration of the male is more vivid.",[30]="To attract females, males dance on the river’s floor. The females gather around the male that dances most gracefully.",[31]="It is the male’s job to make a nest by carving out boulders in a stream using the horn on its head.",[32]="It is the male’s job to make a nest by carving out boulders in a stream using the horn on its head.",[33]="In autumn, its body becomes more fatty in preparing to propose to a mate. It takes on beautiful colors.",[34]="Using its horn, it bores holes in riverbed boulders, making nests to prevent its eggs from washing away."},es={[23]="En otoño, cuando se reproducen, se les puede ver nadando con energía por ríos y arroyos.",[24]="Hace su nido en los agujeros que cava con el cuerno. Defiende sus huevos con su vida.",[25]="En otoño, se ven ejemplares de Seaking macho danzando en las riberas de los ríos para cortejar a las hembras. En esta época, la coloración de este Pokémon alcanza sus niveles máximos de belleza.",[26]="Seaking protege sus huevos con uñas y dientes. Macho y hembra se turnan para vigilar el nido y los huevos. Este período de protección dura más de un mes en el caso de estos Pokémon.",[27]="Cuando las temperaturas bajan mucho, su piel se torna de un color carmesí. Es una señal inequívoca de que se aproxima el otoño.",[28]="Los fanáticos de este Pokémon pueden dividirse en dos grupos: los que adoran sus aletas y los que adoran su cuerno. No se llevan nada bien.",[29]="Es capaz de pulverizar las rocas más duras haciendo girar su cuerno a modo de taladro. Los machos presentan una coloración más viva.",[30]="Los machos ejecutan una coreografía en el lecho del río para ganarse la atención de las hembras, que acuden al mejor bailarín.",[31]="Los machos usan el cuerno de la cabeza para horadar rocas en el lecho del río y construir allí su nido.",[32]="Los machos usan el cuerno de la cabeza para horadar rocas en el lecho del río y construir allí su nido.",[33]="En otoño gana algo de peso para atraer a posibles parejas y se cubre de llamativos colores.",[34]="Perfora las piedras del lecho del río con su cuerno para hacer un nido y que la corriente no arrastre sus huevos."},pt="Com o chifre, faz buracos nas pedras do leito do rio e cria ninhos para que seus ovos não sejam levados pela água."},evo={{s=118},{s=119,from=118,c={{t="level-up",lv=33}}}},moves={[1]={1,64,1,39,1,48,19,48,24,30,30,31,39,127,48,32,54,97},[2]={1,64,1,39,1,48,19,48,24,30,30,31,39,127,48,32,54,97},[3]={1,64,1,39,10,48,15,30,24,175,29,31,41,127,49,32,61,97},